 "about_text": "Ota Fine Arts was founded in 1994 in Tokyo, initially in the Ebisu area, and has long positioned itself as a pioneer of Japanese contemporary art, notably giving early support to Yayoi Kusama. The gallery moved to Roppongi in 2003, relocated to the Tokyo bay area, and returned to a renewed Roppongi space in 2011. It later opened a nearby viewing room, 7CHOME, near the National Art Center. The gallery expanded internationally with a Singapore space at Gillman Barracks in 2012 and a Shanghai gallery in 2017, which reopened in the Rockbund district in 2023. Ota Fine Arts represents artists working in painting, video, craft and installation, with a program emphasizing dialogue among East and Southeast Asian, and more recently Middle Eastern, artists.",
